# The JVM reads .mvn/jvm.config line by line. With CRLF endings each flag arrives as
# "...=ALL-UNNAMED\r", the JVM rejects it as an unknown module, ErrorProne then cannot
# reach the javac internals it needs, and the build fails with an unexplained
# "An unknown compilation problem occurred". Keep it LF on every platform.
.mvn/jvm.config text eol=lf
